{"kind":"report","text":"Planner decision for dc8ff821 (combined Device/archive cohort and G5 first provisioning).\n\nAdopted: the first option. On reviewed G5a main, S2a adds one distinct, explicit combined cohort that speaks both protocols: Register17, Directory16, Rules10 and Destination12, reusing S2a's Membership8. Every shipped or frozen pin keeps its meaning; G5a's reserved and unused Membership9 stays reserved and unused (a reserved number is never reassigned, as the G5a note says); S2a's nine and G5a's numbers stand as 9192ef3f ordered them. The ordinary archive-installation cohort does not learn the Device owner protocol, and the Device cohort does not learn the archive binding: a cohort names exactly the protocols a room speaks, which is the reason the first option is right and the composed alternative is not.\n\nComposition rule. Directory16 is Directory15's data (the Device grant relay) plus the archive slot and bind-archive act of S2a's directories, and Rules10/Destination12 compose the same way; state the rule in S2a's implementation note as a spread order, not a hand merge. S2a's head reruns, on the combined cohort, G5a's core device witnesses (install with the owner grant, open and answer a command) and its own binding witnesses (bind at claim, bind later, install refused unbound then admitted after binding), so the composition is proved not to change either protocol.\n\nSequence. Landing order is G5a, then S2a, then G5's integration head. G5's code and review preparation proceed now against G5a's cohort for the device witnesses, and G5's final head rebases onto S2a's landed main and names the combined cohort in its runbook; the first hosted provisioning of the demo room uses the combined cohort, so plan 033 decision 7 can bind the archive on the running room later without re-founding it. No provisioning on the Device-only cohort.\n\nThe Membership8 omission you found (invitation-key and agent-key client pin lists, CLI directory pairing missing 8 and Directory13/14) is S2a work: correct it in S2a's head with the native person and agent enrolment witnesses, no existing pin changed and no operator custody read.\n\nThis grants no deployment and no source mutation; G5a's sealed views stay read-only.","body":{"to":"builder"}}